[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"morale"
title = "Morale and routing"
order = 110
summary = "Squads break, breaking spreads, and your general is what holds it."
body = "Squads break. Casualties cost morale as a SHARE of the squad, not as a
count of men — losing four out of eight shakes a squad exactly as much as
losing twenty out of forty, so a small elite unit is no braver than a big
cheap one for being small. A squad pushed past its own threshold ROUTS: it stops fighting, runs, and takes
{Combat.PURSUIT_DAMAGE_MULT} times damage while it does. A rout is a defeat,
not a pause — chasing one down is usually worth more than the fight that
caused it.

A squad that breaks costs every ALLIED squad within
{Combat.CHAIN_ROUT_RADIUS_CELLS} cells {Combat.CHAIN_ROUT_MORALE_LOSS}
morale, and one of those can break in turn. Lines do not lose a squad at a
time. They lose a section, and then the rest.

## Your general

Within {Combat.GENERAL_AURA_CELLS} cells of your general, squads recover
morale at double rate and take half the shock when a neighbour breaks. That
is the difference between a line that bends and one that folds, and it is why
he belongs behind the centre rather than out scouting once the fighting
starts.

His death costs every squad in that circle
{Combat.GENERAL_DEATH_MORALE_LOSS} morale. He is a target — theirs, and
yours. Losing him does not lose you the match; it loses you the battle you
were standing in.

## Some troops never break

Troops with no morale to lose cannot be routed by anything: not casualties,
not a flank, not a general dying beside them. The Civilisations page names
which army that is, because it reads it off the troop data rather than being
told."
sources = Array[String](["res://combat.gd", "res://decisions/D-20260819-morale-reads-the-fight.md", "res://decisions/D-20260819-a-general-holds-the-line.md"])
stamp = "c63d5c0177fd254aee6bcab4dd753816f3e449dc115fd7f96e17be5131154f1b"
